{"availability":"available","full":"electric-capital/quest","name":"quest","description":"An open source, self-hosted, safety-focused AI workbench","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":53,"forks":2,"created":"2026-09-21T17:04:22Z","updated":"2026-10-03T01:32:50Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["ai","ai-agents","ai-governance","ai-security","harness","harness-ai"],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z","stars":53,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A self-hosted AI agent workbench: a ChatGPT-style web app where people connect the services they already use (email, documents, Slack, finance tools) and put LLM agents to work on them -- designed so that doing this with sensitive data is safe by default, and usable by people who are not engineers.","Quest runs agentic conversations against multiple LLM providers and gives the agent carefully fenced access to upstream services through per-user OAuth or API keys. Around that core it provides projects with shared workspaces, scheduled routines, a reusable skill library, agent memories, sub-agents, a sandboxed script runner, and admin tooling for credentials, feature gates, model health, and cost reporting.","Models: Anthropic Claude and Google Gemini (both via Vertex AI), plus additional models via OpenRouter (currently DeepSeek and Qwen). Users pick a model per conversation; the LLM provider abstraction makes adding providers and models a registry change."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/electric-capital/quest/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a48dcea2d31c79a8b92dbde52a180501d664c5f94c257d59c4cd545d691c8e36","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T08:36:20.183Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:49.086Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A self-hosted AI agent workbench: a ChatGPT-style web app where people connect the services they already use (email, documents, Slack, finance tools) and put LLM agents to work on them -- designed so that doing this with sensitive data is safe by default, and usable by people who are not engineers.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/electric-capital/quest/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Sign-in is email + password (the default for new deployments, no external setup) or Google OAuth, restricted to an allowed domain or an explicit email whitelist; a password deployment can switch to Google sign-in later and keep every account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/electric-capital/quest/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"outside this repository: how sign-in is set up (the SSO provider, the allowed domain or email whitelist, whether accounts are protected by MFA), how the network is laid out (whether the server is reachable only from a trusted network, what TLS terminates in front of it, what the host can reach), how the Vertex AI and OAuth credentials are scoped, and who holds admin rights.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/electric-capital/quest/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"a48dcea2d31c79a8b92dbde52a180501d664c5f94c257d59c4cd545d691c8e36","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/electric-capital/quest/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:49.086Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T01:32:50Z","overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:42.854Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/electric-capital/quest/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T05:49:49.087Z","hash":"a48dcea2d31c79a8b92dbde52a180501d664c5f94c257d59c4cd545d691c8e36","originalBytes":9548,"storedBytes":9548,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["architecture","docs","quest","oauth","plu